text:
What must be done to make a Play succeed? The common Methods are all over try'd;
We want Assurance to expect Applause ,
Or hope a kind full House without some Cause.
Fain would our Autbress please, and please you so,
That to her self you should the pleasure owe ;
We think she ' s safe by forces of her own ,
And like her Native Ifle depends on none ;
Let her be so by well conducted Scenes,
Nor be secur'd, intrench'd behind Machines ;
Less by a Name from Italy or France,
By Clinch of Barnet, or the Ladder Dance ;
Gladly she does disband all Foreign Aid,
Let Mother Wit defend an English Maid ;
To your own growth for once indulgent prove,
The Manufacture of this Town is Love ;
Love in great Minds bears indisputed way ,
A bapelef Anarchy when that's away ;
The dangerous Paths to Wealth and Fame we tread,
Assur'd the toylsome way to Beauty leads ;
Love and bright Beauty are the Heroes care,
The first learn here, the last view skining there.

blocks.text:
Con. Or as I am to you now;
Mi. Then you'll be new again, like one that has been long out of Print,
and I am always fond of the Second Edition, Revis'd, Corrected and Amended; but be sure you take care never. to let me peruse it thro', reserve something for my Curiosity, Constant; for you know the best Books when we have studied 'em perfectly, are thrown aside, or only kept for Shew, and any trifling Novel that we never met with before, entertains us better.

